  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      213.19,
      397.31,
      238.05
    ],
    "text": "3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      244.15,
      397.21,
      269.01
    ],
    "text": "(a)to ensure the security of the Temple and maintainand development of the Temple;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      275.23,
      397.24,
      299.97
    ],
    "text": "(b)to take action to protect the resident Bhikkhus andto provide their needs;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      306.19,
      397.19,
      342.57
    ],
    "text": "(c)to give assistance for activities aimed at thedevelopment of religious, social and economicaspects of the area around the Temple;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      348.67,
      397.26,
      396.57
    ],
    "text": "(d)while taking action for the stability of the BuddhaDhamma; to take action for the establishment of asociety based on the Buddhist moral value andobserving the five precepts;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      402.67,
      397.34,
      427.53
    ],
    "text": "(e)to make provisions for the achievement of allobjectives expected from a Buddhist Temple;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.15,
      434.71,
      397.31,
      482.49
    ],
    "text": "(f)to establish and maintain institutions for the welfaretraining and rehabilitation of the destitute, thedisabled, the aged, the sick and displaced persons ;and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      489.67,
      397.34,
      526.05
    ],
    "text": "(g)to perform such acts, deeds and things as may benecessary, conducive or incidental to the attainmentof the aforesaid objects of the Corporation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      534.19,
      397.37,
      616.53
    ],
    "text": "4.(1) The affairs of the Corporation shall subject to therules in force for the time being of the Corporation, beadministered by a Board of Management consisting of thePresident, who should be Chief Incumbebt of the Viharayaand Vice President, Secretary, Assistant Secretary, treasurerand five Committee members elected or appointed inaccordance with the rules of the Corporation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      623.71,
      397.28,
      671.49
    ],
    "text": "(2) The first Board of Management of the Corporationshall be the Board of Management of the Society holdingoffice on the day preceding the date of commencement ofthis Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
